From acb7105318130af759d5a0e40418f47660e516c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:43:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] volume-osd: Sliders at the keys' edge, the volume per role
 next to them

The volume keys show a vertical slider at the screen's edge next to the
keys instead of the level bar, as on Android. It changes the output volume,
as the keys do. Swiping it inwards, or the button below it, shows a slider
per role beside it: media, calls, ringtone, notifications, alarm. Each role
plays through a WirePlumber role sink into the output, so its volume is a
share of the output volume: the keys move all roles, the role sliders set
their ratio. Emergency alerts keep their volume. Without role sinks only
the output slider shows. A tap beside it, a swipe outwards or a few
seconds without touching close it.
